WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.042
Hi! Today we'll learn three helpful angle facts. With them, we can find unknown angles.

2
00:00:09.192 --> 00:00:14.538
Fact 1: angles on a straight line add up to 180 degrees.

3
00:00:14.688 --> 00:00:22.818
Here we have 65 degrees and angle a. So a plus 65 degrees equals 180 degrees.

4
00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:29.946
a is 180 minus 65, which is 115 degrees.

5
00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:36.546
Fact 2: angles at a point, all the way round, add up to 360 degrees.

6
00:00:36.696 --> 00:00:45.378
We know 120 degrees and 90 degrees, so x is 360 minus 120 minus 90,

7
00:00:45.528 --> 00:00:49.842
which is 150 degrees.

8
00:00:49.992 --> 00:00:54.594
Fact 3: when two straight lines cross, they make four angles.

9
00:00:54.744 --> 00:01:05.298
The angles opposite each other are called vertically opposite angles, and they are always equal. This one is 40 degrees, so the opposite one is 40 degrees too.

10
00:01:05.448 --> 00:01:15.810
The angle next to it is on the same straight line as 40 degrees, so it's 180 minus 40, which is 140 degrees.

11
00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:23.442
One more: there are three angles on a straight line: 35 degrees, a right angle, and angle y.

12
00:01:23.592 --> 00:01:30.906
A right angle is 90 degrees. So y is 180 minus 35 minus 90,

13
00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:35.034
which is 55 degrees.

14
00:01:35.184 --> 00:01:42.882
Watch out! Some pupils use 360 degrees for angles on a straight line. That is wrong!

15
00:01:43.032 --> 00:01:50.610
A straight line is 180 degrees. A full turn around a point is 360 degrees.

16
00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:58.578
Also, diagrams may not be drawn to scale, so don't guess by looking. Use the angle facts.

17
00:01:58.728 --> 00:02:12.546
Your turn! Four angles at a point are 100 degrees, 85 degrees, 95 degrees and x. What is x? Pause and think.

18
00:02:12.696 --> 00:02:22.074
360 minus 100, minus 85, minus 95 is 80 degrees. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:22.224 --> 00:02:35.850
Another one! Two straight lines cross, and one angle is 73 degrees. What are the opposite angle and the angle next to it? Pause and think.

20
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:49.050
The opposite angle is equal, so it's 73 degrees. The angle next to it is 180 minus 73, which is 107 degrees. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:49.200 --> 00:03:00.786
Last one! Two angles are on a straight line. One is 38 degrees. What is the other? Pause and think.

22
00:03:00.936 --> 00:03:12.594
Angles on a straight line add up to 180 degrees. 180 minus 38 is 142 degrees. Did you get it right?

23
00:03:12.744 --> 00:03:23.970
Remember: angles on a straight line add up to 180 degrees, angles at a point add up to 360 degrees, and vertically opposite angles are equal.

24
00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.314
Now go and practise in your garden!

